la djan cusku di'e:



> ko bevri lei mu djacu lei prenu pe le jubme po'u li ze
> Take the five waters to the people in table 7.
>
> {lei mu djacu} is a collective of five individual waters,
> not a substance.

For lei, yes; I was thinking in loi terms. Part of the trouble
is that piroloi is unique, whereas pirolei is not.

lei is as unique as loi, they are both singular terms, they only
differ in what the underlying set is. You could just as well say:

ko bevri piroloi mu djacu poi cpana le jubme le drata jubme
Take the mass of all five waters on that table to the other table.

mu'o mi'e xorxes




